{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Create a national support system for single disabled parents and their children",
        "additional_details": "Disabled parents can fall between health, social care, childcare and transport services, leaving some without practical support to attend treatment, recover from surgery or safely manage essential parenting responsibilities. As a single disabled mother, I have experienced these gaps first-hand. No parent should have to delay healthcare or risk their health because disability and lack of support leave them with nowhere to turn.",
        "background": "Create a national support system for single disabled parents, including help with childcare during medical treatment and recovery, school and nursery transport, and practical care at home. Ensure disability never leaves a parent unable to access essential healthcare or safely care for their children",
